// Mark II (2026-11-21) = Mark I v1 yang dipangkas ke inti yang dipakai bersama oleh TTrades (Fractal Model), Gareth (GxT) dan Mang Bob:
// sebuah candle HTF menyapu (sweep) candle sebelumnya lalu close kembali ke dalam, candle berikutnya yang ditradingkan, dikonfirmasi oleh CISD.
// Dipertahankan: panel HTF1 (pairing FM) + HTF2 (timeframe sendiri) dengan FVG panel, sweep panel dan high / low candle terakhir; mesin FM CISD
// (C2 / C3, Display Cap, Early CISD, sweep line, label C, Previous EQ, T-Spot, IC-CISD); FM SMT dengan SATU simbol (chart + panel HTF1);
// PSP (HTF1 + HTF2, Confirmed / Live); Vertical Lines, HTF Open, Open Lines, Daily / Weekly Open; status bar.
// Dibuang dari Mark I: Formation Liquidity, Key FVG + SMT Fill, HTF Candle SMT, Strength Switch, SMT Fill panel, HTF2 SMT / SS,
// simbol SMT 2 dan 3 (tanpa request), Key Levels + HTF1 Pane Range, MMXM, Daily 50%.
// [Mark II b] Opsi HTF1 Fractal = FM memakai pairing sistem 1m→15m, 3m→15m, 5m→1H, 15m→4H, 30m→4H, 1H→7H, D→W, M→3M.
// [Mark II c] Label C2 dari setup tidak valid = ✕ merah (warna Invalid): xC2 saat C3, atau wick yang kemudian mengambil extreme C2 (protected swing hilang).
// [Mark II d/e] Setelah C2 diambil belakangan (✕ merah, satu ukuran lebih besar), label C3 / C4, IC-CISD, kotak T-Spot dan Previous EQ dari setup itu disembunyikan; garis CISD-nya tetap sampai setup yang lebih baru mengambil slot Display Cap.
// [Mark II g] Waktu garis vertikal kembali ke HH:mm untuk setiap jam (18:00, bukan 18).
// [Mark II i] HTF Candle SMT kembali untuk satu simbol SMT: panel HTF1 (dan panel HTF2, toggle sendiri), Live / Confirmed, Lookback 1-3, Cap; close melewati extreme SMT menghapus garis yang tersimpan. Tanpa request tambahan.
// [Mark II j] SMT = Chart / Pane / Both / Off (Pane juga menggambar HTF Candle SMT di panel HTF1; HTF2 Candle SMT dibuang); simbol Second SMT opsional (satu request tambahan hanya saat aktif); satu simbol -> label SMT, dua -> nama pasangan.
// [Mark II k] xC2: C3 merah ikut disembunyikan (hanya ✕ merah yang tersisa); warna default Vertical Lines hitam dengan opacity 29%.
// [Mark II l] SMT Fill kembali hanya di panel HTF1 (opsi Fill di baris Candle SMT): SMT antara dua candle panel berurutan di dalam FVG panel yang masih hidup, garis titik-titik A -> B, kotak gap lalu disembunyikan. Tanpa request tambahan.
// [Mark II m] SMT Fill punya baris sendiri: toggle, warna, gaya garis, lebar.
// [Mark II ae] Time in Body dibuang; semua default input disesuaikan dengan screenshot referensi pengguna (Status Bar Bottom Right, Session Levels off, SS off, HTF2 PSP off, Candle SMT Confirmed / Lookback 1 / HTF2 on, Label Chart Tiny, Last Candle H/L off, Daily / Weekly Open off, C-Labels Both, ...).
// [Mark II ah] Garis EQ HTF3 membawa label '0.5 D' / '0.5 W' di ujung kanan, diwarnai menurut candle pemilik EQ (bullish #089981, bearish merah).
// [Mark II aj] Grup HTF3: PDH / PDL (PWH / PWL di Weekly) seperti Session Levels: 1-2 candle HTF3 terakhir yang sudah selesai, belum tersapu = solid ke kanan dengan nama, tersapu = berhenti di bar penyapu (gaya swept, nama di awal garis). Ada gaya Unswept / Swept sendiri, Swept Labels, Sets; set yang lebih lama bernama PDH-2 / PDL-2.
// [Mark II aj] Merapikan menu: HTF2 Open Time dipindah ke bawah baris HTF Label, 'Previous EQ: Draw On' ke bawah baris Previous EQ, 'HTF2 PSP (HTF2 Pane)' ke bawah baris PSP. Logika tidak berubah.
// [Mark II ai] HTF2 = 4H / 6H: waktu open ditulis 2 digit (18 22 02 06) agar label tidak saling menumpuk; 7H tetap HH:mm.
// [Mark II ag] Waktu open HTF2 (7H / 4H / 6H) berada dalam satu baris di bawah low terendah panel HTF2 (tidak ada lagi label bertumpuk); toggle baru HTF2 Open Time (4H / 6H), 7H tetap menampilkan waktunya.
// [Mark II af] Panel HTF3 (Daily / Weekly, grup 5.1): candle seperti panel lain, garis titik-titik open / high / low + harga OHLC (candle berjalan), EQ titik-titik (candle sebelumnya + candle ekspansi terbaru), dan pembacaan fase per candle menurut Mang Bob / Gareth (Accumulating / Manipulating / Distributing? / Distributing / Expanding / Failed; chart <= 15m). Tanpa request tambahan.
// [Mark II ad] HTF2 = 4H atau 6H: candle panel menampilkan waktu open New York di bawah candle, seperti panel 7H (setiap candle; tanpa pengecualian candle pendek).
// [Mark II o] PO3 A / M / D dibuang; candle panel 7H menampilkan waktu open New York (18:00, 01:00, 08:00; bukan candle pendek 15:00) menggantikan A / L / N.
// [Mark II p/q] Pairing Range (2D): -R / +R = high / low dari 2 hari trading NY terakhir yang sudah selesai, tetap sepanjang hari; hanya di chart.
// [Mark II s] Session Levels (grup 9 baru): high / low dari sesi Asia, London, NY AM dan NY PM terakhir (jam dan timezone sendiri); belum tersapu = solid ke kanan dengan nama, tersapu = berhenti di bar sweep dengan gaya swept. Chart intraday sampai 1H, tanpa request.
// [Mark II t] SMT: tag '2S' pada label C2 dari setup dua tahap (SMT C1->C2 plus SMT C2->C3 atau PSP di C2 / C3); Strength Switch 'SS' di panel HTF1 (sisi yang lebih kuat dari SMT / PSP terakhir berbalik dalam N candle); label PSP diwarnai menurut arah (close chart naik / turun).
// [Mark II u] Request simbol SMT tanpa calc_bars_count (opsi itu hanya menyimpan bar terakhir sebelum hari ini, sehingga Bar Replay tidak punya SMT / PSP / SS).
// [Mark II v] Status bar: '(no data)' setelah simbol SMT yang request-nya tidak mengembalikan apa pun di bar terakhir.
// [Mark II w] Symbol Data = HTF1 (default): simbol SMT di-request pada timeframe HTF1 (HTF2 PSP pada timeframe HTF2), sehingga Bar Replay menyimpan SMT / PSP / SS jauh ke belakang (histori intraday simbol kedua pendek). Chart = request lama pada timeframe chart.
// [Mark II x] Session Levels: level yang tersapu tidak punya nama secara default (toggle Swept Labels), nama hanya di tepi kanan.
// [Mark II y] Session Levels: nama level yang tersapu berada di awal garisnya (di atas high, di bawah low); Swept Labels aktif secara default.
// [Mark II z] Expansion EQ di panel HTF1: EQ dari candle ekspansi terbaru, dipertahankan sampai ada close di luarnya.
// [Mark II z2] Expansion EQ digambar seperti Previous EQ (warna, gaya, lebar, sampai candle berikutnya + 2 bar, tanpa label).
// [Mark II aa] Key Levels dari Mark I kembali (-TF / +TF dari panel tertinggi yang tampil, di chart); Pairing Range (2D) dibuang.
// [Mark II ab] Candle SMT HTF2 (toggle, default off): HTF Candle SMT di panel HTF2, mode / Lookback / Cap yang sama, high / low ditambahkan ke request HTF2 PSP.
// [Mark II ac] (Time in Body, dibuang lagi di ae)
// [Mark II C1-C2] Potongan mandiri dari Mark II: panel HTF + mesin FM dengan C1 / C2 (label C3 / C4 off), CISD, sweep line, Previous / Expansion EQ, T-Spot, IC-CISD, garis vertikal, open, key levels. SMT, PSP, Strength Switch, Session Levels, HTF3 / PDH dan status bar dihapus dari menu (dikunci off).
// Riwayat step sebelum Mark II: lihat Mark I v1 (step 72).

//@version=6
indicator("Mark II C1-C2", overlay=true, max_lines_count=500, max_labels_count=500, max_boxes_count=500, max_bars_back=5000)
import Gregorius_XV/GXVUtils/10 as QTU

//==============================================================================
// Deklarasi waktu
//==============================================================================
tf_sec = timeframe.in_seconds(timeframe.period)
TF_SEC_60 = timeframe.in_seconds("60")
TF_SEC_240 = timeframe.in_seconds("240")
TF_SEC_D = timeframe.in_seconds("D")
TF_SEC_W = timeframe.in_seconds("W")
TF_SEC_M = timeframe.in_seconds("M")

// [FM step 2] Helper timeframe: 7H ('420', dari pasangan 15m-7H) ditangani di sini, selebihnya oleh library
const string TF_7H = '420'
const int TF_7H_SEC = 25200
f_htf_seconds(string tf) =>
    tf == TF_7H ? TF_7H_SEC : QTU.htfSeconds(tf)
f_htf_label(string tf, bool src) =>
    tf == TF_7H ? '7H' : QTU.htfSourceLabel(tf, src)

//==============================================================================
// Grup (step 26: urutan menu = Timeframes, FM, SD, penanda waktu, panel, SMT, SMT-Fill / Sequence, range, status bar, performa)
//==============================================================================
gHTF = "1. Timeframes"
gCISD = "2. FM Model"
gFMLv = "3. FM Levels"
gTM = "4. Time Markers"
gHTFSetings = "5. HTF Pane Visuals"
gH3 = "5.1 HTF3 (Daily / Weekly)"
gSMT = "6. SMT / PSP"
gSMTSym = "7. SMT Symbol"
gStatus = "8. Status Bar"
gSess = "9. Session Levels"
gSessApp = "9.1 Session Appearance"
gPerformance = "10. Performance"
//==============================================================================
// Input
//==============================================================================

// 1. TIMEFRAME
htf1_fractal_input = input.string('Automatic', 'HTF1 Fractal', options = ['Automatic', 'FM', 'Custom', '3m-30m', '5m-1H', '15m-1H', '30m-4H', '1H-4H', '1H-7H', '4H-1D', '1D-1W'], group = gHTF, tooltip = 'FM pairing for HTF1 (the CISD model runs on HTF1, also when the HTF1 pane is hidden). Pairs from the materials only (step 54, Gareth / Mang Bob): W <- D swing, D <- 4H swing, 4H / 7H <- 1H / 30m swing, 1H <- 15m swing (PO3 slide), 1H / 30m executed on 5m / 3m.\n\nAutomatic: 3m→30m, 5m→1H, 15m→1H, 30m→4H, 1H→4H, 4H→D, D→W (other chart timeframes: no model, use Custom).\nFM (Mark II system pairing): 1m→15m, 3m→15m, 5m→1H, 15m→4H, 30m→4H, 1H→7H, D→W, M→3M (other chart timeframes: no model).\nCustom: HTF1 TF Source.\nA fixed pair needs a chart timeframe below its HTF, otherwise HTF1 is off.')
htf_sweeps_tf_1_custom_tf = input.string('1h', 'TF Source', options = ['3m', '5m', '15m', '30m', '90m', '1h', '2h', '3h', '4h', '6h', '12h', 'D', '3D', 'W', 'M', '3M', '6M', '12M'], group = gHTF, active = htf1_fractal_input == 'Custom')
htf_sweeps_tf_1_show = input.bool(true, 'Show HTF1 Pane', inline = 'TF1_pane', group = gHTF)
htf_sweeps_tf_1_number = input.int(7, 'Candles', minval = 1, maxval = 60, inline = 'TF1_pane', group = gHTF, active = htf_sweeps_tf_1_show)
htf_sweeps_tf_2_show = input.bool(true, 'Show HTF2 Pane', inline = 'TF2_pane', group = gHTF)
htf_sweeps_tf_2_number = input.int(4, 'Candles', minval = 1, maxval = 60, inline = 'TF2_pane', group = gHTF, active = htf_sweeps_tf_2_show)
htf_sweeps_tf_2_custom_tf = input.string('7h', 'HTF2 Timeframe', options = ['5m', '15m', '30m', '1h', '90m', '2h', '3h', '4h', '6h', '7h', '12h', 'D', '3D', 'W', 'M', '3M', '6M', '12M'], group = gHTF, active = htf_sweeps_tf_2_show, tooltip = 'Fixed timeframe for HTF2 (does not follow the chart timeframe). The HTF2 pane is hidden when the chart timeframe is not below it. It is shown whatever HTF1 is. 7H only: the New York open time under the pane candles (18:00, 01:00, 08:00; none on the short 15:00 candle).')
htf_custom_daily_open = input.bool(false, 'Custom Daily Open        ', inline = 'customdaily', group = gHTF)
htf_custom_daily_time = input.string('Midnight', '', options = ['Midnight', '18:00'], inline = 'customdaily', group = gHTF)

// 2. MODEL FM
cisd_show = input.bool(true, 'Enable CISD', inline = 'CISD', group = gCISD, tooltip = 'FM rules on the HTF1 timeframe (also when the HTF1 pane is hidden). Level = open of the opposing candle run traced back from the C2 extreme; triggers on a body close through it in C2 (once the sweep is back inside) or in C3; no trigger by the C3 close = dropped. Until C3 closes: C3 closing back beyond the swept C1 level, or a C3 wick beyond the C2 extreme (protected swing), voids the setup and hides its CISD.')
cisd_display_cap = input.int(1, 'Display Cap', minval = 1, maxval = 50, group = gCISD, active = cisd_show, tooltip = 'How many of the newest setups whose C2 has closed with a CISD keep their line (newest C2 first, both directions). 1 = a new setup removes every older CISD. A setup that turned void / xC2 still uses its slot and draws nothing, so older lines do not come back. A CISD still forming inside C2 is drawn on top and does not count.')
cisd_bull_clr = input.color(color.new(#2962ff, 0), '', inline = 'CISD', group = gCISD)
cisd_bear_clr = input.color(color.new(#cd0030, 0), '', inline = 'CISD', group = gCISD)
cisd_line_width = input.int(2, 'CISD Line Width', minval = 1, maxval = 5, group = gCISD, active = cisd_show)
cisd_early_show = input.bool(true, 'Early CISD', inline = 'ECISD', group = gCISD, active = cisd_show, tooltip = 'On the running (not yet closed) chart bar: the price is already through the CISD level of a live setup (in C2 also back inside the swept level). Drawn dashed until the bar closes; the CISD only counts on the close.')
cisd_early_line_style_input = input.string('Dashed', 'Style', options = ['Solid', 'Dashed', 'Dotted'], inline = 'ECISD', group = gCISD, active = cisd_show and cisd_early_show)
cisd_early_line_width = input.int(1, 'Width', minval = 1, maxval = 5, inline = 'ECISD', group = gCISD, active = cisd_show and cisd_early_show)
cisd_early_line_style = cisd_early_line_style_input == 'Solid' ? line.style_solid : cisd_early_line_style_input == 'Dotted' ? line.style_dotted : line.style_dashed
fm_sweep_where = input.string('Both', 'Sweep Line', options = ['Chart', 'Pane', 'Both', 'Off'], inline = 'sweep', group = gCISD, tooltip = 'Step 58 (Chart Sweep Line + Pane Sweep in one). Chart: the swept C1 level of the FM setups (those holding a Display Cap slot, plus a live C2), from the C1 high / low to the C3 open (to the running bar while C2 runs). Pane (step 69): HTF1 and HTF2 alike, the newest sweep of the pane candles (a candle takes the high / low of the previous one and closes back inside; gone once a later candle closes beyond it), from the swept wick to the running candle + 2 bars, label = pane timeframe. Both = chart + panes. The last closed candle high / low in the panes has its own toggle in Key Levels.')
bool fm_sweep_show = fm_sweep_where == 'Chart' or fm_sweep_where == 'Both'
bool pane_sweep_show = fm_sweep_where == 'Pane' or fm_sweep_where == 'Both'
htf_sweep_color = input.color(#000000, '', inline = 'sweep', group = gCISD, active = fm_sweep_where != 'Off')

// 3. LEVEL FM
fm_lbl_where = input.string('Both', 'C-Labels', options = ['Chart', 'Pane', 'Both', 'Off'], group = gFMLv, active = cisd_show, tooltip = 'Where the C1-C4 labels go: Chart = on the chart, Pane = on the HTF1 pane candles (when the HTF1 pane is shown), Both, Off. Step 49. Labels on the wick of each candle of the setups whose CISD uses a Display Cap slot: C1 at the swept high / low, C2 at the C2 extreme, C3 / C4 on the edge of their T-Spot (bottom = bullish, top = bearish, one bar right of its left side; chart only), otherwise at the high (bearish) or low (bullish) of that candle. They stay when the setup turns invalid, until a newer setup takes the slot. Invalid colour: C2 + C3 on xC2 (C3 beyond the C2 extreme), C3 when C3 closed back beyond the swept C1 level, C4 on xC4 (C4 beyond the C3 extreme).')
bool fm_lbl_show = fm_lbl_where != 'Off'
bool fm_lbl_chart = fm_lbl_where == 'Chart' or fm_lbl_where == 'Both'
bool fm_lbl_pane = fm_lbl_where == 'Pane' or fm_lbl_where == 'Both'
fm_lbl_c1 = input.bool(true, 'C1', inline = 'CLBL', group = gFMLv, active = cisd_show and fm_lbl_show, tooltip = 'C1 shows in the HTF1 pane only (step 67: never on the chart).')
fm_lbl_c2 = input.bool(true, 'C2', inline = 'CLBL', group = gFMLv, active = cisd_show and fm_lbl_show)
fm_lbl_c3 = false  // [Mark II C1-C2] fixed (input removed)
fm_lbl_c4 = false  // [Mark II C1-C2] fixed (input removed)
fm_lbl_size_input = input.string('Tiny', 'Size', options = ['Tiny', 'Small', 'Normal'], inline = 'CLBL2', group = gFMLv, active = cisd_show and fm_lbl_show)
fm_lbl_size = fm_lbl_size_input == 'Normal' ? size.normal : fm_lbl_size_input == 'Small' ? size.small : size.tiny
fm_lbl_valid = input.color(#000000, 'Valid', inline = 'CLBL2', group = gFMLv, active = cisd_show and fm_lbl_show)
fm_lbl_invalid = input.color(#F23645, 'Invalid', inline = 'CLBL2', group = gFMLv, active = cisd_show and fm_lbl_show)
fm_eq_show = input.bool(true, 'Previous EQ', inline = 'PEQ', group = gFMLv, active = cisd_show, tooltip = 'EQ of the previous candle, for the valid setups that use a Display Cap slot with a triggered CISD: C2 EQ across C3, C3 mid across C4. C2 EQ (step 51): sweep wick bigger than the body -> middle of the sweep wick (low to the lower body edge for bullish, high to the upper body edge for bearish), otherwise (high + low) / 2. C3 and the running-candle EQ always use (high + low) / 2. The HTF2 pane also shows the C2 EQ across the running C3 of its newest swing (Draw On Both / HTF Pane). On the running candle the line already reaches its end (the next vertical line). On xC4 (C4 beyond the C3 extreme) the C3 mid stops at that bar in the Invalid C-Label colour. None for void / xC2 setups. The mid of the previous HTF1 candle is also drawn across the running HTF1 candle, with or without a setup. HTF1 pane: from the wick of the previous candle to the end of the candle + 2 bars.')
fm_eq_color = input.color(color.new(#000000, 0), '', inline = 'PEQ', group = gFMLv, active = cisd_show and fm_eq_show)
fm_eq_style_input = input.string('Dotted', '', options = ['Solid', 'Dashed', 'Dotted'], inline = 'PEQ', group = gFMLv, active = cisd_show and fm_eq_show)
fm_eq_style = fm_eq_style_input == 'Solid' ? line.style_solid : fm_eq_style_input == 'Dashed' ? line.style_dashed : line.style_dotted
fm_eq_width = input.int(1, 'Width', options = [1, 2, 3, 4], inline = 'PEQ', group = gFMLv, active = cisd_show and fm_eq_show)
fm_eq_where = input.string('Both', 'Previous EQ: Draw On', options = ['Chart', 'Pane', 'Both'], group = gFMLv, active = cisd_show and fm_eq_show, tooltip = 'Chart: Previous EQ on the price chart. Pane: on the HTF1 pane candles (when the pane is shown). Both: chart + pane.')
xeq_show = input.bool(true, 'Expansion EQ (HTF1 Pane)', inline = 'XEQ', group = gFMLv, tooltip = 'Mark II z. EQ (high + low) / 2 of the newest expansion candle in the HTF1 pane: body at least half of its range and a close beyond the previous candle (bullish: above its high, bearish: below its low). Same look as Previous EQ (its colour, style, width): from its wick to the end of the next candle + 2 bars, no label. Removed once a later closed candle closes beyond it (continuation failed: Mang Bob / Gareth 50% rule). Not drawn when it is the previous candle (Previous EQ already shows it).')
fm_ez_show = input.bool(true, 'Entry Zone (T-Spot)', inline = 'EZ', group = gFMLv, active = cisd_show, tooltip = 'FM T-Spot for C3 and C4 of the valid setups that use a Display Cap slot (none for void / xC2). EQ zone = candle open <-> EQ (C3: the C2 EQ, step 51 = middle of the sweep wick when the wick is bigger than the body, else the full C2 range; C4: the full C3 range); valid only when the EQ is below the open (bullish) / above it (bearish). CISD zone = CISD level <-> CISD 50% (mid of the bodies from the CISD candle to the C2 extreme). Overlap -> from the open to the far edge of the overlap, else the EQ zone. Grows with the running candle, stops at its end; the C4 box is removed on xC4.')
fm_ez_bull = input.color(color.new(color.rgb(41, 98, 255), 96), 'Bullish', inline = 'EZ', group = gFMLv, active = cisd_show and fm_ez_show)
fm_ez_bear = input.color(color.new(color.rgb(242, 54, 69), 96), 'Bearish', inline = 'EZ', group = gFMLv, active = cisd_show and fm_ez_show)
fm_ic_show = input.bool(true, 'IC-CISD', inline = 'IC', group = gFMLv, active = cisd_show, tooltip = 'FM IC-CISD: same-side CISDs after the main CISD body break, through the end of C4 (stops on xC2, void, xC4). Starts on the next opposite candle (level = its open, re-traced on every new extreme like the main CISD); confirmed by a close through the level after the extreme bar when a 3-candle swing exists in that run. Line from the start candle to the confirm bar (CISD colours / width), dot on the swing. Grey once a wick trades beyond the dot. Drawn for the setups whose CISD is shown. A new IC-CISD after a T-Spot touch makes that T-Spot CONFIRMED.')
fm_ic_dot_input = input.string('Tiny', 'Dot', options = ['Tiny', 'Small', 'Normal', 'Large'], inline = 'IC', group = gFMLv, active = cisd_show and fm_ic_show)
fm_ic_dot = fm_ic_dot_input == 'Small' ? size.small : fm_ic_dot_input == 'Normal' ? size.normal : fm_ic_dot_input == 'Large' ? size.large : size.tiny

// 4. PENANDA WAKTU
vl_show = input.bool(true, 'Vertical Lines', inline = 'VL', group = gTM, tooltip = 'Vertical line at the open of the last HTF1 candles, from the lowest low to the highest high of those candles. Text above: weekday for Daily and higher with the regular open, otherwise the open time HH:mm (New York), also for the 18:00 Custom Daily Open. ▾ marks the C2 open of the setups that use a Display Cap slot. The text sits just above that high; Text Offset raises it by average bars (14-bar mean high-low range).')
vl_color = input.color(color.new(#000000, 71), '', inline = 'VL', group = gTM, active = vl_show)
vl_count = input.int(6, 'Count', minval = 1, maxval = 50, inline = 'VL', group = gTM, active = vl_show)
vl_size_input = input.string('Small', 'Text Size', options = ['Tiny', 'Small', 'Normal'], group = gTM, active = vl_show)
vl_size = vl_size_input == 'Normal' ? size.normal : vl_size_input == 'Tiny' ? size.tiny : size.small
vl_txt_color = input.color(#000000, 'Text', inline = 'VLT', group = gTM, active = vl_show)
vl_txt_off = input.float(0.5, 'Text Offset (bars)', options = [0.0, 0.5, 1.0, 2.0], inline = 'VLT', group = gTM, active = vl_show)
vl_gap = input.int(6, 'Min Label Gap (bars)', minval = 0, maxval = 200, group = gTM, active = vl_show, tooltip = 'Step 66: a time label closer than this many bars to the last label shown is skipped (its line stays); the newest label and a C2 open (▾) always show. 0 = every label.')
ho_show = input.bool(true, 'HTF Open', inline = 'HO', group = gTM, tooltip = 'Horizontal line at the open of the running HTF1 candle, from its first bar on the chart to that candle in the HTF1 pane (to the last bar + 1 when the pane is hidden). Step 45 (restored).')
ho_color = input.color(color.new(#9598A1, 0), '', inline = 'HO', group = gTM, active = ho_show)
ho_style_input = input.string('Solid', '', options = ['Solid', 'Dashed', 'Dotted'], inline = 'HO', group = gTM, active = ho_show)
ho_style = ho_style_input == 'Dashed' ? line.style_dashed : ho_style_input == 'Dotted' ? line.style_dotted : line.style_solid
ho_width = input.int(1, 'Width', options = [1, 2, 3], inline = 'HO', group = gTM, active = ho_show)
ol_show = input.bool(true, 'Open Lines', inline = 'OL', group = gTM, tooltip = 'Horizontal line at the open of the last Count candles of Open TF (4H = 18 / 22 / 02 / 06 / 10 / 14 New York for gold and futures; HTF1 = the FM model timeframe). The running candle: solid to the last bar, label = its open time. Older opens: dotted and fainter, each stops at the end of the next candle so it does not run over current price. Replaces HTF Open (step 36).')
ol_color = input.color(color.new(#9598A1, 0), '', inline = 'OL', group = gTM, active = ol_show)
ol_tf = input.string('4H', 'Open TF', options = ['4H', 'HTF1'], inline = 'OL', group = gTM, active = ol_show)
